2.In Android Studio, open the Plugins section and install the Flutter and Dart plugins. Restart the IDE and verify that both plugins are enabled in the settings.

Step 1 — Open Plugins
In Android Studio:
File → Settings → Plugins

On macOS:
Android Studio → Settings → Plugins

Step 2 — Install Flutter
Select the Marketplace tab.
Search for Flutter.
Click Install.
Android Studio may also ask to install the Dart plugin.
Accept/install it.

Step 3 — Restart Android Studio
Click Restart IDE when prompted.
If you aren't prompted, close Android Studio and open it again.

Step 4 — Verify both plugins
Go back to:
Settings → Plugins → Installed
Search for:
        Flutter
        Dart
